From 25f5fd8a169612a74ec3100160395f82a418b43f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:07:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Let players edit their own sheet, logged for the
 Lightkeeper

Issue #64, decision 1 of fix round 5 (detection, not prevention). A new
edit_sheet message stores any change a player makes to their own sheet
(name and words, role and specialty, abilities, ratings and gilds, drives,
maximums, resistances, marks, scars up to three) with only shape checks.
update_gear no longer refuses a player's change (unmarking, past the
slots, One Step Ahead's object). A player's pip set by hand, a gear change
and an edit each write one line for the Lightkeeper and the player
("Mara: Nerve 2 to 3.") and set characters.sheet_edited, the roster card's
dot, which gm_sheet_seen clears. member_status carries the name so a
rename reaches the other members' cards.

Checked: new tests/test_ws_sheet_edits.py; the flipped gear and drive
tests in test_ws_character.py; test_surface, test_00_startup (fresh
database), test_access, test_ws_circle, test_ws_marks, test_ws_gm_view,
test_ws_connect pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ETKqHLvkfH9k99JTnJzzKA
